by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of northeast and east central Colorado, including\nthe following areas; the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer\nDivide area, and portions of the northeast and east central plains\nincluding Elbert, Lincoln, eastern Adams and Arapahoe, Washington,\nMorgan, Logan, and northeastern Weld Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Thunderstorms with heavy rain, combined with recent rainfall and\nsaturated soils in some locations, will bring a threat of flash\nflooding into this evening. The greatest threat will be shifting\nslowly east and northeast across the plains. Stronger storms will\nbe capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30 minutes, with\nlocal storm totals as high as 3 inches.","ends":"2026-08-14T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e10de82f1876e978fca96f676db0545b1a5d765e.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e10de82f1876e978fca96f676db0545b1a5d765e.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 14 at 7:10PM MDT until August 14 at 10:15PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorth Central Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1015 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 710 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This may cause small\nstream flooding. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.5 inches are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nAkron, Midway and Fremont Butte.","ends":"2026-08-14T22:15:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d79167e89afa4f6b6677164ab61591c8d4e4362b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d79167e89afa4f6b6677164ab61591c8d4e4362b.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-14T23:49:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 142349 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 549 PM MDT Fri Aug 14 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Daily chances for thunderstorms with heavy rainfall capable of producing flash flooding for burn scars and urban areas expected through Sunday and possibly even Monday. - Flash Flood Watches expanded to include El Paso County through this evening, and another Flas","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-14T17:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 141709 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1109 AM MDT Fri Aug 14 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-151715- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?sit